### <a id="_Toc237556002"></a>User Scope

The proposed system is intended for independent game developers and small development teams who manage various digital assets such as images, audio files, scripts, and other game resources. The system supports multiple user roles, including system administrator, workspace owners, workspace managers, and collaborators, allowing users to work together within a shared environment. Users can upload, organize, and manage digital assets within a centralized platform, as well as search, access, and retrieve assets efficiently to support their development tasks. In addition, the system enables collaboration among users by allowing them to share assets and interact through commenting features on asset pages, where team members can provide feedback and discuss improvements to enhance coordination during development. Furthermore, users can view and manage asset version history, allowing them to track changes and maintain consistency during collaborative workflows. The system is limited to registered users only and is designed primarily for small to medium\-scale development teams. It does not target large enterprise\-level organizations or support large\-scale multi\-organizational collaboration.

The objective of the proposed system is aimed at independent game developers and small development teams that handle a wide range of digital assets such as images, audio files, scripts, and other game development resources. The system offers the possibility of multiple user roles, including system administrator, workspace owner, workspace manager, and collaborator, allowing users to work in a common environment. The users can upload their digital assets in organized and managed ways in a single place, search the necessary assets, access them, and retrieve the assets needed for their work. The system also allows users to communicate with each other through the asset pages by leaving comments and exchanging their opinions about the assets to improve the development process and enhance communication in the team. The platform also allows users to use the version history of their assets and keep their work organized while cooperating with the members of their teams. The system cannot be used by the users that are not registered and it is designed primarily for small to medium\-scale development teams. It does not target large enterprise\-level organizations or support large\-scale multi\-organizational collaboration.

