## <a id="_Toc237556028"></a>Rapid Application Development (RAD)

Rapid Application Development (RAD) is a software development methodology that focuses on fast system development through iterative prototyping and continuous user feedback (Lal, 2024). The technique promotes adaptability and fast implementation of functioning systems instead of adopting a rigid and direct development approach. RAD makes it possible for developers to create system components gradually, introducing improvements thanks to the received feedback, making it a perfect method for the projects requiring constant changes.

